 "section_summary": "This section contains the concluding analytical narrative and comprehensive statistical reference tables of a GHQ/SCAP Natural Resources Section report examining Japan's agricultural experiment station system. The text evaluates historical advances in rice, wheat, and tea breeding, crop disease mitigation for wheat stripe and snow blight, and the correlation between chemical fertilizer applications and unit-area crop yields, concluding with an administrative appraisal that recommends consolidation, improved inter-prefectural research coordination, and reorganized farmer education to maximize food production. The accompanying tables present an exhaustive national directory of Imperial, prefectural, educational, and private agricultural, sericultural, and livestock research facilities, followed by statistical compilations on station facilities, operational budgets, staffing, cooperative projects, and historical production trends from 1878 to 1946.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "A comprehensive GHQ/SCAP Natural Resources Section report reviewing the history, breeding achievements, disease control programs, facilities, and administration of Japan's agricultural experiment station system, accompanied by detailed directory and statistical tables.",
