   "start_page": 60,
   "summary": "This report analyzes the contributions and organization of agricultural research in Japan, tracing historical breeding breakthroughs in rice and wheat varieties, management strategies for devastating crop diseases such as wheat stripe and snow blight, and the direct dependence of crop yields on commercial and organic fertilizer supplies. It critically reviews the proliferation and administrative fragmentation of prefectural and Imperial experiment stations, recommending administrative consolidation under qualified technical directors, enhanced inter-prefectural problem-oriented coordination, and the reform of farmer education and extension services to overcome postwar food shortages. The document concludes with an exhaustive national directory and extensive statistical tables detailing the facilities, staffing, budgets, and cooperative research projects of Imperial, prefectural, academic, and private agricultural stations, alongside historical production and acreage data for rice, wheat, barley, tea, and sericulture from 1878 to 1946.",
   "title": "The Agricultural Experiment Stations of Japan",
   "to": ""
  }
